# Compiler and EBNF

Core owns the Adaptive Script / expression **compiler runtime** under `src/afw/compile/` (separate from interface-based extension APIs). Public API and compile types: **`afw-compile`**.

## Source of truth
- Grammar fragments live in C comments marked `/*ebnf>>>` … `<<<ebnf*/` beside the real parser (mainly `compile/afw_compile_parse*.c`, `compile/afw_compile_lexical*.c`).
- `src/afw/generate/ebnf/*.txt` is **not** the grammar: first non-comment line is the output basename; following lines are source globs to scan (e.g. `syntax.txt` → `syntax.ebnf`).
- `afwdev generate` harvests into `src/afw/generated/ebnf/` (e.g. `syntax.ebnf`). Derived docs only; W3C-style and explicitly imprecise.
- Handbook diagrams under `src/afw/doc/syntax/` are maintained from that harvest.

## Where productions live (edit C + EBNF comment together)

| Concern | Primary file |
|---------|----------------|
| Tokens / residual | `afw_compile_lexical.c` |
| Symbols / contextual | `afw_compile_parse.c` |
| Script / TestScript / statements | `afw_compile_parse_script.c` |
| Expressions / operators / lambdas | `afw_compile_parse_expression.c` |
| JSON / literals | `afw_compile_parse_value.c` |
| Templates (`#{…}` / `${…}`, TemplateString) | `afw_compile_parse_template.c` — compile-time nested script is isolated (`parent=NULL`); `\#`/`\$` suppress openers |
| Destructuring | `afw_compile_parse_assignment_target.c` |

## When changing the language
1. Edit the EBNF comment blocks and the real parse/lex C.
2. Change `generate/ebnf/*.txt` only if which files are scanned (or the output name) must change.
3. `./afwdev build --cdev -j`

## Do not
- Hand-edit `generated/ebnf/`.
- Treat harvested EBNF as executable truth — the C parser is.
- Assume a top-level `parenthesized` / `parentheses` compile type (dead docs only; it was an internal expression production, never wired as a `-s` value or compile type enum). See `afw-command` and `afw-compile`.
